# Worksheet content conventions

When creating or editing worksheet JSON in `backend/data/worksheets/`:

## Difficulty and question count

All questions in one worksheet use the same `"stars"` value (1, 2, or 3). Question count depends on difficulty:

| Stars | Difficulty | Questions |
|-------|------------|-----------|
| 1 | easy | **25** |
| 2 | medium | **20** |
| 3 | hard | **15** |

Filename: `questions_N.json` (stem = worksheet id).

## Reading (english)

- Use `"passages"` with `"body"` (not `"text"`).
- Split questions evenly across passages (e.g. 20 Q → 4×5, 15 Q → 3×5, 25 Q → 5×5).
- Vocabulary / inference focus; match difficulty to stars.

## Multiple choice

- Shuffle `"choices"` so the correct `"answer"` is not always first — spread across positions B/C/D.
- Every `"answer"` must exactly match one choice string.

## Other fields

- Include `"created_at"` (ISO) for Latest tab sorting.
- `"subject"`: `math`, `english`, `science`, `data`, or `general`.
- Math worksheets: `"scratchpad": true` unless reading-only style.
- **Save progress:** only on **non-timed** worksheets (server draft). Students use **Save progress** / **Save & exit** on the worksheet page.
- **Timed worksheets:** set `"timed": true` and `"time_limit_minutes"` (positive integer). Save is disabled; timer starts on first open and auto-submits at zero. Leaving before submit **locks** the worksheet until an admin unlocks it. Listed under **Timed** on the student home (not Latest).
- **Data analysis** worksheets: use `"subject": "data"`. Scratch pads stay available but are **hidden by default** (students can turn them on). Chart/table passages below.
- NCERT-based worksheets: set `"content_badge": "NCERT"` (shown before the subject badge).
- **Latest tab:** worksheets appear for 14 days from `sort_ts`. Portal upload sets `sort_ts` to upload time; bundled JSON uses `created_at` (or file mtime).

## Data passages (charts & tables)

Reading worksheets can include visual data in `passages[]`:

- **`body`** or **`text`** — intro (optional if `chart` or `table` is present)
- **`chart`** — `{ "type": "bar"|"line"|"pie", "labels": [...], "values": [...], "title"?, "xLabel"?, "yLabel"? }`
- **`table`** — `{ "headers": [...], "rows": [[...], ...] }`

Link questions with `"passage_id"`. Labels and values must match in length; values are numbers ≥ 0.
